                        <tr>
                           <th>Conclusion and Recommendations based on this report and previous findings known to us:</th>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                           <td>Renal function is mildly decreased (GFR 63 mL/min/1.73 m²), consistent with stage 2-3a chronic kidney disease. Urine albumin/creatinine ratio is at the upper limit of normal (28 mg/g), suggesting possible early kidney involvement. Recommend monitoring renal function and albuminuria, and addressing cardiovascular risk factors.</td>
